{
  "request": {
    "model": "nomic-embed-text:latest",
    "input": [
      "Synthetic nurse note for software testing. No real patient data.\n\nIn a commercial-driver follow-up arranged after an occupational screening concern, the nurse interviews the driver and checks the accompanying documents against the reported sequence of events; the employer wants a quick answer before allocating a vehicle, but the record separates present evidence, historical findings and questions that the clinician has not yet resolved.\n\nThe current GP and medication review confirm established type 2 diabetes managed by diet and exercise alone, with no glucose-lowering medicine or insulin prescribed, and document that driving-relevant comorbidities have been assessed with no disqualifying effect; the driver mentions that an uncle uses injections, but those medicines belong to the uncle, and a previous referral proposing tablets was never implemented as a current treatment change.\n\nThe usual work involves coupling trailers, checking mirrors, interpreting radio messages and responding to pedestrians in a loading area, with breaks that can be delayed when deliveries run late; the driver explains which difficulty occurred while stationary and which was noticed during ordinary duties, rather than claiming that quiet conversation in the clinic reproduces every task in the cab.\n\nThe record is prepared for the reviewing clinician with the sequence of events and the provenance of the available findings intact, because the employer summary and the driver's account answer different questions; a completed test is retained as such, but an unresolved detail is not filled in from a family member's history or from an earlier document with different testing conditions.\n"
    ],
    "truncate": false
  },
  "provider_called": true,
  "status": "completed",
